1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
In this tutorial, we'll cover how to set up agents in Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:22,560
So I'm logging in as an administrator, and to configure agents, we go to Options and Agents.

3
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:28,920
Here we can see the agent machines that have been set up in this installation of Burp Suite

4
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:29,920
Enterprise Edition.

5
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:34,720
So we have one agent machine which is running on the server itself, and we have another agent

6
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:38,120
machine which is running on an external server.

7
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,120
You can add as many agent machines as you need.

8
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:45,680
You can also configure the count of agents that are running on each machine.

9
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,240
And again, you can bump up or adjust the number of agents that are running on any machine very

10
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,280
easily.

11
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:58,540
The number of agents determines the number of concurrent scans that this machine can perform

12
00:00:58,540 --> 00:00:59,540
at any time.

13
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:04,780
If you intend to perform a large number of scans in parallel, you will typically need

14
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:09,120
to create a number of agent machines and configure them.

15
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:13,720
There are system requirements for agent machines, and these depend on the number of agents that

16
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:16,360
you intend to run on the machine.

17
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,980
Please refer to the product documentation for more details of those.

18
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:23,540
So let's see how you add a new agent machine.

19
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:30,400
Now I'm on a different server where I plan to install a Burp Suite Enterprise Edition agent.

20
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:35,740
Enterprise Edition can run on Windows, Linux, or Mac OS, and you can have a mix of different

21
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,540
operating systems in your installation if you wish.

22
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:45,540
So I'm going to show an installation on Windows.

23
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:59,540
So I'm running the installer, and I'm going to select to just install the Enterprise Agent.

24
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:07,120
I need to tell it the hostname or the IP address of the server which is running Burp Suite Enterprise

25
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:12,020
Edition.

26
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:16,660
You need to configure details of the database that you are running in your installation.

27
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:20,980
For this installation, we're using the embedded database which is suitable for evaluation or

28
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,540
proof of concept purposes.

29
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:31,260
The installer then shows us the fingerprint for this agent.

30
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:35,300
So in a moment we'll go back to Enterprise Edition server and we will see an authorization

31
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,220
request from this agent with this fingerprint.

32
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:42,200
So you should make a note of this fingerprint and verify that the authorization request came

33
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,200
with the right one.

34
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:50,860
So that's everything that we need to do on the agent machine to make the installation.

35
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:56,660
So if we go back to the web interface for the Enterprise Edition UI, we can now see we have

36
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,780
an authorization request pending.

37
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:03,560
And we can see the fingerprint of the public key that was displayed while we were installing

38
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,440
on the agent machine.

39
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:09,580
So now we simply need to authorize this request.

40
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:13,800
Now we can see that the new agent machine has appeared in the list and it's available for

41
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,800
scanning.

42
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:20,020
At this point, I can set the number of assigned agents for this machine.

43
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:27,020
And if I wish, I can give this agent a more convenient name.

44
00:03:27,020 --> 00:03:34,340
At the bottom of this page, we can see the total number of agents that we have assigned.

45
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:40,900
And we can see the number of unassigned agent licenses that are available to be assigned.

46
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:45,520
So Enterprise Edition is licensed by the number of agents that you have.

47
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:49,680
This means the number of concurrent scans that you could perform.

48
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:53,760
If in your scan list, you see entries showing waiting for agent, this means that you've

49
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,520
reached the limits of the number of agents that you have.

50
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:58,520
And you can resolve that by adding more agents.

51
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:02,520
Burp Suite Enterprise Edition's licensing model is extremely flexible.

52
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:06,520
It lets you scan as regularly as you wish and across your entire estate.

53
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:10,520
There are no limitations on the number of URLs, the number of domains or servers that you can

54
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:15,520
scan, just the number of concurrent scans depending on the number of agents that you have.

55
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:22,520
So that's how to set up agents in Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

